\f0\b \cf0 \strokec2 Topic 4: Failure Mode Analysis
\f1\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Summary:
\f1\b0  A data-driven analysis was conducted on the 260 failed runs to document exactly how the small (8B) model breaks when operating without external context. \
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Results:
\f1\b0  The analysis revealed three primary failure modes:\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl1
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Parametric Knowledge Exhaustion:
\f1\b0  This was the leading cause of errors (65.8% of all failures). The model lacked the stored knowledge of specific exact numbers (like policy limits or stipends) and hallucinated incorrect numeric values. \
\ls4\ilvl1
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Few-Shot Contamination (Overfitting):
\f1\b0  The Few-Shot strategy suffered the highest failure rate (87.50%). The model overfit to the provided examples, actively copying numbers and phrases from the prompt's examples instead of answering the user's actual query. \
\ls4\ilvl1
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Ungrounded CoT Verbosity:
\f1\b0  While Chain-of-Thought and Decomposition scored highest, they resulted in highly verbose failures (averaging 728.3 characters) where the model confidently detailed step-by-step logic that was based on completely fabricated premises. \
